{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Hard-reset this instance to canon: hardreset.sh made mechanical as a detached runner sharing the update_crates machinery (same rundir/status file, so the two pipelines mutually refuse to stack; poll dev.dev.update_crates_status, which reports kind:hardreset and steps:6). Steps: (1) guarded git clone of canon into CHUCKTHIS - nothing destructive happens unless the clone succeeds, (2) overlay canon src/data/newbound_core/Cargo.toml over the instance and purge generated sources (Cargo.lock, src/lib.rs, src/{app,dev,peer,security}, cmd; rustup update tolerated-fail), (3) build the canon binary inside the clone, (4) newbound rebuild and (5) newbound recompile THROUGH that canon binary - the new-code-runs-the-rest principle - then the clone is deleted, (6) final feature-matched host build; restart verdict by host-binary hash. Local/overlay libraries are untouched (canon data/* replaces only canon libs). Sets the hotswap_paused gate for the duration. NOTE: FFI crate pins are NOT rewritten - if canon's flowlang/ndata pins moved, crate_versions will report mismatch after restart; run update_crates at the new versions to align them. The instance keeps serving OLD code during the run; avoid store edits while it runs. Callable on a peer via /peer/remote/uuid/dev/hard_reset.","groups":"admin","import":"use flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse crate::dev::dev::compile::build_compile_command;\nuse std::fs;\nuse std::process::Command;\nuse std::process::Stdio;\n","params":[{"desc":"Git URL of the canon repo to reset from. Empty string uses the default https://github.com/mraiser/newbound.git. Restricted to [A-Za-z0-9._/:@+-] because it is interpolated into the runner script.","name":"url","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"lwnwig1a052f17ecdt4","readers":["admin"],"time":1788097976208,"username":"system","writers":[]}